From d3684a35e7fa9e1af784c5ee53d2c397cd37dbf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soaresden <soaresden@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:15:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] j2me: point MIDP 2.0 getWidth/getHeight calls at Canvas
 on install

Darkest Fear 1 and 2 (Rovio) are MIDP-1.0 games, but they were compiled
against the MIDP 2.0 classes. Their two calls to getWidth() and
getHeight() therefore name Displayable, which has these methods only
since MIDP 2.0. The S60v1 VM that KMidRun runs has them on Canvas only,
so the game exits at the first call: the VM writes
"ALERT: Unhandled FatalSlotError" to stderr and terminates.

When KMidRun installs a JAR, each class is now checked for method
references to Displayable.getWidth()I or Displayable.getHeight()I.
Such references are pointed at a Canvas class constant, which is reused
if the class already has one, or else appended to the end of the
constant pool. Canvas has both methods in MIDP 1.0 and 2.0. The JAR is
then written back as a zip. A JAR that needs no change is still copied
byte for byte.

common::archive gains read_archive(), which reads every entry into
memory, and write_zip_archive(), which uses libarchive's zip writer with
deflate and no padding after the end of central directory record.
